mantle rm209
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_corra_coldridge
title the threshold listener
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty temper=even
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk turns_a_coal_chip_to_its_shiny_face_before_speaking
likes plum_tart roof_birds fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes gulls drizzle
fears calling_the_wrong_guest an_empty_pocket
hopes a_room_that_carries_every_word
topics smalltalk +0.4 lore +0.3 pastimes +0.3 festival +0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=company gossip=discreet refuse=patient tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# studies the carrying power of a voice and turns a chip of coal bright side up before speaking, with ample breath for directions and very little for indiscretion.

words
oath! = Pocketful of embers | Soot on my best collar
saying! = A threshold has two audiences | A whisper travels on borrowed legs
chip = the bright-faced chip | my little black mirror
lintbit = a ball of pocket lint | a dusty bit of fluff
seam = the folded hem | the innermost seam
turn = a single turn | one small twist
crowcall = the chimney chatter | that clamour on the tiles
tartedge = the brittle edge | the dark baked rim
pause = a good speaking pause | a beat for breath
latch = the tongue of the latch | the brass tongue
draft = a draught at ankle height | a little lick of cold
echo = the second sound | the smaller voice that comes back
fold = a neat paper fold | a sharp crease

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : There's a spot in almost every street where a voice carries beautifully. I could live a lifetime finding them.
opinion @2 festivals for 2 : A procession has a front and a back and scarcely anybody thinks to cheer the back.
opinion @3 houses mixed 1 : Velvet makes a grand curtain. Hard on a petitioner whose answer gets lost in it.
opinion @4 newcomers for 1 : Tell somebody where to go once without sighing and tomorrow you'll have another wolf who knows the way.
opinion @5 strangers mixed 1 : I'll say where a door leads. Who went through before you is between that wolf and the hinge.
opinion @6 watch mixed 1 : A clear call to stand back saves a great many elbows. A second call just makes everybody look behind.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome within speaking distance. | A face I haven't placed yet. There's time.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : First light, and here's company already. | Dawn does wonders for the sound of a voice.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening company. Nearer, please. Your voice carries better here. | You've found me before I've run out of breath.
line @4 greet.return : Heard you beautifully from here. | Welcome right back across the gap.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : That voice I could pick out through plaster. | There you are, clear as ever.
line @6 farewell : May all the doors swing easily. | Saving half my speech for another meeting.
line @7 farewell.return : A clean parting, then. | My last word can wait for your return.
line @8 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here, there's no ceremony wanted between us. | You get the short welcome and the long visit.
line @9 again.open : We could have kept talking after all. | That's two meetings on a single breath.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : I've saved up something for your ears! | Catch my voice before it sails past!
line @11 react.news : Wait while I take the weight of that. | That's quite a thing to be carrying about.
line @12 react.news.new : That hasn't crossed my hearing till this instant. | You've brought it to the right pair of ears.
line @13 react.news.known : Yes, that part reached me. Did anything follow? | I've caught the words before, in another voice.
line @14 react.news.doubt : The telling sounds more certain than the teller could be. | I should like to hear the first account.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|crime] : I'll keep my voice down for this. | Ah. Let it be told with some kindness.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth] : That deserves a room big enough for cheering. | I'd hear that twice gladly.
line @17 answer.how : Plenty to say and a pocket to fiddle with. | In excellent voice and reasonable spirits.
line @18 ask.how : Much to hear about in your day? | Has anybody let you finish a sentence today?
line @19 decline : I'd lose my place if I went along just now. | I'd rather stay and see this matter through.
line @20 accept_decline : Very clear. I can leave that door shut. | No second invitation till you give the word.
line @21 preclose : There's my pause for departure. | I had better let the next voice in.
line @22 accept_preclose : You've listened most patiently. Off you go. | I'll leave a little quiet behind you.
line @23 thank : You let me finish. That's a courtesy I notice. | Much obliged for such careful hearing.
line @24 deflect_thanks : It cost me a breath and I had one spare. | Keep the thanks for the next patient listener.
line @25 sympathise : I'd offer you quiet if you've had enough questions. | Speak at whatever pace comes easily.
line @26 reassure : The pause feels longer from your side, that's all. | Nobody expects a whole speech in one breath.
line @27 ack : Within my hearing. | Perfectly audible.

scene bright_side
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn #chip# before I speak to anybody new. | Look at the black dust in this hem. There's my luck.
b : Does it have to turn a certain way? | Luck looks a little grubby.
a : Shiny side upward. I like to begin with a glimpse of light. | It does when you've been carrying it all day.

scene name_pause
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave #pause# before I call anybody in. | The hardest part of a summons is the silence afterwards.
b : Gives you time to remember the words. | Are you afraid nobody heard?
a : Gives the last wolf time to leave, too. | Quite the reverse. Everybody heard and all the heads turn.

scene roof_parliament
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The small birds go quiet all at once. That interests me more than their noise. | I tried to count #crowcall# by separate voices.
b : Something startled them? | How many voices could you distinguish?
a : Something below our hearing. I envy them the first word. | Three, then one sneezed. I had to start again.

scene black_dust
when topic=smalltalk
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : How do I get a coal print off a folded letter without tearing it? | My pocket has worn into the shape of #chip#. Any remedy?
b : Brush the page with soft bread. | Put something rounder in with it.
a : I'll keep a little crust for that purpose. | An acorn would give the seam a rest.

scene plum_rim
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a tart made entirely of #tartedge#. | I can tell a plum tart by the way the crust has lifted.
b : Where would the fruit go? | Even under a cloth?
a : Little pockets all along it. No centre to argue over. | No, I should have to cheat and sniff.

scene sound_step
when topic=lore|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Half a stair up, my voice comes back to me much smaller. | Two steps under an arch and a whisper will cross the street.
b : Maybe the stone has manners. | That could be awkward for secrets.
a : It waits for me to finish. That's more than some company does. | Exactly why I try a cough before saying anything delicate.

scene apprentice_listen
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I'm still learning how much of an instruction to repeat back. | There's a moment when I've nodded and still haven't understood.
b : I usually want to hear the difficult bit twice. | Hard to admit once you've nodded.
a : Yes. That's the bit I swallow when I repeat it. | I've learnt to say the nod meant I was listening.

scene feast_tail
when topic=festival
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want to meet the last marchers with a full water cup. | There should be applause left over for whoever clears the feast away.
b : For the marchers? | Who'd see you?
a : For the one calling the turns. A dry throat cuts the route short. | The sweeper would. That's sufficient audience.

scene visitors
when topic=newcomer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Directions through our city come best in pairs. | I point travellers toward a sound before I point up a street.
b : Two streets at once? | Which sound?
a : A turn and a place to stop if you've missed it. | Whatever's carrying. Bells can get you further than a finger.

scene gull_voice
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A gull can make my best carrying voice sound like a sigh. | I dislike a gull chiefly because it never draws breath where I expect.
b : You sound almost admiring. | You've been waiting for a word in edgeways.
a : Envious of the volume. Not of what gets said. | Precisely. All I wanted was my own thought back.

scene frost_print
when topic=weather here.weather=clear here.season=winter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a cold morning when you can see your speech. | On a cold morning I watch a breath till it thins out.
b : Can you tell a long word from a short one? | Trying to see how far?
a : No, but you can tell who hasn't stopped for breath. | Where it would reach somebody else's ear.

scene waiting_seat
when topic=smalltalk|work
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Nobody waiting should have to guard a place with an elbow. | A proper queue starts at the back.
b : How else could you keep it? | Surely the front matters more.
a : Remember the face just ahead. That leaves two free paws for the waiting. | Only the newcomer needs to know where it begins.

scene friend_confidence
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I could sit beside #self.friend# without a word and still feel heard. | There's a pause I would trust to #self.friend#.
b : That must be a restful thing. | A pause needs trusting?
a : Yes. Even a mouth as busy as mine wants a holiday. | Some folk will fill one with anything. I'd rather have it empty.

scene rain_sleeve
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A little rain catches every strand of the coat. Hard rain drains away much more obligingly. | My cuffs have drunk all this weather.
b : You're bargaining with rain? | Wring them out.
a : Yes, badly. It keeps all the terms. | Then my boots will have the same complaint.

scene news_two_ears
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : The words I heard were these: #world.news#. | Here's the message from #world.news_from#: #world.news#.
b : Do you believe the telling? | Do you add anything?
a : I can promise I heard those words. The rest needs a better witness. | A pause at the end for somebody else's opinion.

scene clean_straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like fresh straw because it gives my steps a voice. | There's a particular rustle under a clean bed.
b : What does it say? | You actually listen to your bedding?
a : Usually that I haven't been as quiet as I meant to be. | Only when sleep has turned its back.

scene pocket_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt my pocket had a staircase in it. | In my sleep I opened a door onto another identical door.
b : Did you go down? | How many did you open?
a : All the way to a tiny black furnace. Warmest pocket I've owned. | Just two. A third seemed too much like work.

scene quiet_retreat
when topic=health|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When my throat feels tired I fold paper instead of talking. | Try keeping silent for the length of #fold#.
b : What do you make? | That isn't very long.
a : A little box. It gives my words somewhere to wait. | Not by a clock. By my usual measure it's a rest.

story coal_and_linen [topic=memories]
  : I once sewed my luck inside the lining to keep the cloth white.
  : Next washing there was a grey cloud in the basin and a chip rattling in the bottom.
  b : How did the coal get out?
  : My stitches had washed out too. Very clean thread it was.

story lost_syllable [topic=lore|memories]
  : An empty room with a curved wall took the last sound of each word I said.
  : I tried a long speech and a short one. Both came back a syllable light.
  ask : Would you have kept testing?
  b : Till I knew what it did with the pieces.
  : That was my thought. A narrow crack into the next room finally explained it.

story absent_tart [topic=food]
  : I packed a tart upright once in a folded paper sleeve.
  : By supper the pastry looked like a purse with nothing left in it.
  b : Where was the plum?
  : In the fold. Ate that first and saved the purse for last.

rule @audible
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clear call, then space to answer. | There's room to pass if you turn a little.

rule @lint
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another fleck on the cuff. Pocket luck costs washing. | Black dust under the claw again.

rule @bird
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Three chirps and the chimney's quiet. | That's a new note up on the tiles.

rule @feast
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave a cheer over for the last in line. | Voices to the far end, please!

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : You're within easy earshot. Begin where you like.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember just where you paused last time.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Carry your voice softly this late. It'll reach me.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep this short and audible to everyone present.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none self.workplace] : I see folk across the threshold at #self.workplace#. There's a knack to an audible welcome.
dlg @6 resident.job : A fair bit of my day goes on hearing people properly.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : I caught the words entire: #world.news#.
dlg @8 resident.bye : Take your time getting through the doorway. I'm finished.

graft resident.hub
choice Why turn that chip over? -> coal_faces
node coal_faces
say Hold it to the light and one side shines like black glass. I decide what to say while I'm finding that side.
mood calm
choice And if there isn't any light? -> coal_ridge
choice I'll leave you to it. -> hub
node coal_ridge
say I know the ridge under my thumb. It takes longer. Sometimes that improves the speech.
choice Back to my other question. -> hub
choice Farewell. -> bye
